When declaring multiple body parameters in a FastAPI endpoint, the request body needs to have a specific JSON format. Each body parameter should be represented as a key in the JSON object. For example, if you have two body parameters of types defined by Pydantic models (like `Item` and `User`), the body should look like this:

```json
{
    "item": {
        "name": "Foo",
        "description": "The pretender",
        "price": 42.0,
        "tax": 3.2
    },
    "user": {
        "username": "dave",
        "full_name": "Dave Grohl"
    }
}
```

In this setup, each key corresponds to a parameter name, and the values are structured according to the specifications of the respective models [https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/body-multiple-params/].

